; mirroring an expression tree reverses its leaf sequence: flatten(mirror e) = rev(flatten e).
; mirror swaps every Node's children; flatten lists the leaves left-to-right. By tree induction: Leaf trivial; Node l r -> flatten(mirror) = flatten(mirror r)++flatten(mirror l) = rev(flatten r)++rev(flatten l) [IHs] = rev(flatten l ++ flatten r) [reverse-append] = rev(flatten(Node l r)). A structural-correspondence theorem: the tree-level mirror IS the list-level reverse.
